.\" mount_ufsbe.8 — manual page for the mount_ufsbe(8) helper
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 11, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_UFSBE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_ufsbe
.Nd mount a UFS1/UFS2 filesystem via ufsbe
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Ar special
.Ar mountpoint
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a thin wrapper around
.Xr ufsbe 8
that conforms to the interface expected by
.Xr mount 8 .
.Pp
When
.Xr mount 8
is invoked with
.Fl t Cm ufsbe ,
or when an
.Xr fstab 5
entry specifies filesystem type
.Cm ufsbe ,
.Xr mount 8
calls
.Pa /usr/local/sbin/mount_ufsbe
with the same arguments:
.Pp
.Dl mount_ufsbe [-o options] special mountpoint
.Pp
.Nm
forwards all arguments unchanged to
.Xr ufsbe 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
See
.Xr ufsbe 8
for a description of supported
.Fl o
mount options.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Mount a UFS2 partition using
.Xr mount 8 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# mount -t ufsbe /dev/ada0s1a /mnt
.Ed
.Pp
Mount read-only:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# mount -t ufsbe -o ro /dev/ada0s1a /mnt
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr mount_fusefs 8 ,
.Xr ufsbe 8
